Epictetus told his students to have these ready on every occasion (Handbook 51):

- Cleanthes's prayer, "Lead me, Zeus, and you, Destiny," wherever you have set me; I will follow willingly, and if I would not, I would follow anyway.

- "If it pleases the gods, so be it" (Socrates to Crito).

- "Anytus and Meletus can kill me, but they cannot harm me" (Socrates at his trial).$q$, 65, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true),
