Seneca wrote as a man still in training, writing to a friend in training. His rules come from the Letters to Lucilius (Gummere's translation, cited by letter number) and his essays (Stewart's translation): On Anger, On Benefits, On Providence, On Peace of Mind, and On the Shortness of Life.$q$, 49, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true),
