- Hold every hour in your grasp. Do today's work today and you will depend less on tomorrow. While we postpone, life speeds by. Time is the only thing that is truly ours, and we let anyone take it (Letters 1).

- Live each day as if it completed your life. Every day should be arranged as though it closed the series and rounded out your existence (Letters 12).

- Stop complaining that life is short. Life is long enough if you know how to use it. We are not given a short life; we waste a long one on greed, useless busyness, wine, sloth, and ambition (On the Shortness of Life 1 to 2).

- Fear the thought of death, not death. Death is always the same distance away. What we fear is our idea of it (Letters 30).$q$, 136, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true),
