- Alternate solitude and company. Solitude cures us when we are sick of crowds, and crowds cure us when we are sick of solitude (On Peace of Mind 17).

- Let the mind relax. It should not always be strained to the same pitch. Socrates played with little boys, Cato refreshed his mind with wine after affairs of state, and Scipio danced. Seneca even allows wine now and then to wash away cares, adding that moderation is wholesome both in freedom and in wine (On Peace of Mind 17).$q$, 87, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true),
