- Be good now. Do not act as if you had ten thousand years. Death hangs over you. While you live and while you can, be good (IV.17).

- Take troubles one at a time. Do not think about all the troubles of your whole life at once. Ask of the present one, "What here is unbearable?" and you will be ashamed to answer. Only the present can hurt you, and it is small (VIII.36).$q$, 73, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true),
