- He stood thinking from one dawn to the next. At Potidaea he stood lost in thought through a whole day and night, then prayed to the sun and walked away (Symposium 220c to 220d).$q$, 34, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$unverified$q$]::text[], true),
