From the Arete corpus: Plato, Apology and Gorgias, trans. Benjamin Jowett; Xenophon, Memorabilia, trans. H. G. Dakyns. The final section draws on Plato's Symposium, Laches, Crito, and Phaedo and Xenophon's Apology, none yet in the corpus.

The section on a Socratic life in modern terms also draws on Seneca's Letters, On Providence, and On Anger; Epictetus's Discourses and Handbook; Marcus Aurelius's Meditations; Cleanthes; and Musonius Rufus. The feats section adds Diogenes Laertius VI, Xenophon's Symposium, and Plutarch's Cato the Younger. Its verdicts on modern activities are applications of their principles, not their words.$q$, 93, $q$original$q$, $q$https://github.com/Kylejemery/arete-app/blob/main/academy/corpus-ingestion/synthesis/virtues-of-socrates.v1.md$q$, 2026, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$synthesis$q$, $q$english$q$, $q$Intermediate$q$, array[$q$corpus_verified$q$]::text[], true)
